./docs/scratch/arrival-break/slice1-panel-synthesis.md:43:**Forward costs**: B FORECLOSES OUTER-SIGNED TICKS as written. libs/custody/src/custody/signing.py has an explicit guard — 'An empty observer must never sign: keys_root / "" collapses to the flat layout, which would mint the VERTEX key's authorship claim for an anonymous writer' (signing.py ~135-141, `if not observer or '..' in observer.split('/'): return None`). If ticks ever gain outer signatures, an empty-observer tick returns None from the signer by design, and B + tick signing become mutually exclusive without reworking that guard. This makes B and the second agenda item structurally coupled: choosing B is choosing to close the tick-signing door, not merely defer it. rows[0] wart: INHERITED. Dual-signature principle: neutral, same as A. Git-diff readability: a genesis line has no 'who' outside the envelope and a tick body is {name, payload} — under B a raw tick line's observer column reads as empty, so the name is still visible inside body but the column is dead weight. Global relax (variant ii) also removes the rule that currently prevents an empty observer on genesis/fact/batch/key even though no mint site passes one — a weakening with no compensating benefit.
