     1	"""arrival_head_attestation — remembering a lineage's head across opens.
     2	
     3	Slice 3 of the arrival break (``design:arrival-break-slice3-witness-minimum``).
     4	The design of record is ``docs/scratch/arrival-break/slice3-design-proposal.md``
     5	§§A-C; the protocol it implements a minimum of is
     6	``docs/architecture/arrival/witness-protocol.html``.
     7	
     8	**What this module is for.** A backend can prove a log is internally consistent
     9	— genesis validates, every record links to its predecessor, the head is the
    10	last one. It cannot prove that the log in front of it is the *same* log this
    11	machine accepted yesterday, because every fact it could consult lives inside
    12	the boundary an attacker or a restore would move. So the memory of what was
    13	accepted has to live somewhere a single restore of the store cannot also
    14	revert, and comparing the two is what turns "this log is well-formed" into
    15	"this log is the one we know".
    16	
    17	**stdlib and** :mod:`engine.arrival_contract` **only.** Not a taste rule: this
    18	journal exists to stay readable when the store it witnesses cannot be opened at
    19	all, and a module that dragged the file codec and sqlite3 behind it would tie
    20	its own readability to the health of the thing it is judging. The classifier is
    21	pure, the journal is ``pathlib``/``json``/``os``, and
    22	``test_reading_a_head_journal_does_not_drag_the_adapter_in`` pins it.
    23	
    24	**The name is the Rule 18 join.** ``arrival*.py`` under ``engine/`` is globbed
    25	by ``test_every_arrival_named_engine_module_is_scanned``, so naming the module
    26	this way enrolls it in the arrival vocabulary ratchet by birth rather than by a
    27	``_SCAN_TARGETS`` edit somebody has to remember.
    28	
    29	**Vocabulary hazard.** "Attestation" already means something else here:
    30	``FactAttestation``/``TickAttestation`` are the *signed* receipt on a committed
    31	row. What this module writes is unsigned and local, so its serialized ``type``
    32	is ``arrival-head-observation`` — distinct types, distinct serialization names
    33	— which also leaves the future signed corpus unencumbered. Nothing here is
    34	signed: no ``sig``, ``issuer``, ``key_id`` or chaining field, and their absence
    35	is the point rather than an omission. An empty ``sig`` field would advertise a
    36	claim this slice does not make.
    37	
    38	**What is deliberately not here.** The seam that calls this on every open, the
    39	evidence gatherer that walks a backend for descent, the audit and trust-reset
    40	producers, and staleness reporting are WP3's. The conformance vectors are
    41	WP2's. This module holds the record, the journal, and the judgment.
    42	"""
