   694	@dataclass(frozen=True)
   695	class HeadLowerBound:
   696	    """*K* is **at least** this, because the read was INCOMPLETE.
   697	
   698	    **"Incomplete read" is this module's one term for the weakening
   699	    condition, and this is its definition:** the read needed something it did
   700	    not get — a line it could not parse, a line it could not classify, an
   701	    entry written by a later build, or the header itself. :attr:`JournalRead.skipped`
   702	    :attr:`skipped` records every skip, and the WEAKENING ones — every cause
   703	    except a literal re-assertion — are what produce this type.
   704	    Prose here has drifted four times by naming one cause as though it were
   705	    the definition (unreadable lines, then damage past the last line, then a
   706	    missing header); the term is deliberately about what the read LACKS
   707	    rather than about why, so that a new cause joins it without new
   708	    vocabulary.
   709	
   710	    Not "unreadable" — that word belongs to text this build cannot read at
   711	    all (:class:`JournalUnreadable`, :class:`HeadUnreadable`), and a journal
   712	    with a missing header and every entry readable is incomplete without
   713	    being unreadable in any part. Not "unaccounted" either: :func:`unaccounted_heads`
   714	    already means heads the STORE can no longer account for, a different
   715	    question about a different party.
