  1194	def parse_journal_lines(lines: Iterable[str]) -> JournalRead:
  1195	    """Read a journal from its raw lines. Pure — no filesystem.
  1196	
  1197	    The pure half is separate so the conformance vectors can hand it raw log
  1198	    lines and so every read rule is testable without a temporary directory.
  1199	
  1200	    **Every line this build cannot use is skipped and reported, wherever it
  1201	    sits** — which is half of what makes a read incomplete
  1202	    (:class:`HeadLowerBound`); a missing header is the other half. The
  1203	    earlier design distinguished a torn final line from damage further up and
  1204	    refused the latter, on the reasoning that skipping could silently lower
  1205	    *K*. Skipping CAN lower *K* — concurrent writers journal out of order, so
  1206	    the epoch maximum is not the last line and damage anywhere can take it
  1207	    (``finding:s3wp1-epoch-ordinals-do-not-ascend-in-file-order``). But
  1208	    refusing was the wrong answer to it. It made an ordinary crash a permanent
  1209	    incident, and it claimed a protection this location cannot deliver: anyone
  1210	    who can corrupt a line here can delete the whole journal instead and be
  1211	    met with trust-on-first-use. So the loss is **carried in the result type**
  1212	    — :class:`HeadLowerBound` — rather than converted into a verdict, and the
  1213	    positional rule dissolves along with the distinction it enforced.
