1. PASS — Amendment #4. Mutating `re_asserted()` to add weakening weight made the crash-retry regression and mixed-cause regression fail: 2 failed. The duplicate permanently produced `HeadLowerBound`, as intended by the mutation demonstration.

2. PASS — Amendment #5. Removing position scoping made both targeted regressions fail: damage behind the reset remained bounded, and the mixed-side test counted two weakening skips instead of one.

3. PASS — dedup predicate under acceptance load. `_scan()` compares `line.strip()` text at [arrival_head_attestation.py:1123](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops-s3wp1/libs/engine/src/engine/arrival_head_attestation.py:1123). Thus byte-different lines can match only through leading/trailing JSON whitespace; that whitespace carries no JSON claim. Internal whitespace variants and Unicode-normalization variants do not compare equal. All production journal writers pass through canonical `_entry_line()`.

The acceptance backstop holds on every production ADVANCED path: the sole production classifier path calls `_descent()`, which performs full verification and resolves the remembered coordinate before `compare()` can return ADVANCED ([arrival_head_seam.py:1131](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops-s3wp1/libs/engine/src/engine/arrival_head_seam.py:1131)). The injected-collision test and abandoned-backup seam test both passed. “Byte-identical” is slightly imprecise terminology because surrounding whitespace is stripped, but no distinct claim can strip-collide.

